guide forever/horde/40-50/02-feralas
title Feralas & Tanaris
faction Horde
levels 42-44
zone Feralas
next forever/horde/40-50/03-feralas
# Route from the Polestar route simulator's Horde consensus (Tauren export),
# visits 33-38, levels 42.5-44: Tanaris, Feralas, then the way back east.
# Checked by lint, not play-tested on Forever yet. Era + known Forever quests
# only.
#
# Flow: Misty Reed Post (where the previous guide ends) -> fly Stonard to
# Grom'gol -> zeppelin to Orgrimmar (training, riding; Druids and Paladins:
# Thunder Bluff for training; Warlocks: Ratchet for the Felsteed) -> fly
# Freewind Post -> Gadgetzan (flight path) -> eastern
# Wastewander camps -> Gadgetzan -> southern Wastewander camps ->
# Steamwheedle Port -> Lost Rigger Cove -> Steamwheedle Port -> Gadgetzan ->
# fly Freewind Post -> Camp Mojache (flight path, bind) -> Woodpaw north camp
# and the Gordunni Outpost -> Mojache -> sprite darters and Woodpaw alphas ->
# Mojache -> Grimtotem camp and the Woodpaw battle map -> Mojache -> one
# sweep west: the Writhing Deep, the southern Gordunni ruins, the Rogue Vale
# screechers and, with the distress beacon, OOX-22/FE's escort -> hearth
# to Camp Mojache (every hand-in) -> fly Orgrimmar (Ripple Recovery, training) -> zeppelin
# to Grom'gol -> fly Stonard, where the next guide starts.
#
# Deviations from the simulator's order:
# - Tanaris: Gadgetzan's two bounty quests are done in the camps east and
#   south of town before Steamwheedle Port, so Lost Rigger Cove is one sweep
#   and the visit ends at the Gadgetzan flight master.
# - Feralas: hub-batched loops out of Camp Mojache (north; west and south;
#   then one sweep from the Writhing Deep west, re-seeded for flow in 0.3.5:
#   the southern ruins waited for a Mojache return of their own, and the
#   Writhing Deep had one too). The beacon drops from any Feralas mob, so
#   there is no ride to the Forgotten Coast for it. The hearthstone to Camp
#   Mojache is used after the escort (it ends on the far west coast).
# - Binds: Gadgetzan, Thunder Bluff, the Undercity, Grom'gol and Booty Bay
#   are dropped: each is replaced before any hearth uses it. Camp Mojache is
#   kept for the hearth after the escort.
# - Dropped stops (each a flight, zeppelin or boat for a few small quests):
#   Thunder Bluff for The Black Shield (1276, 1400 XP); the Undercity for
#   Apothecary Zinge's errands and Patrick Garrett (232, 238, 243 Into the
#   Field and 2342 Reclaimed Treasures: 780 XP here, the rest much later);
#   the Booty Bay stop of visit 38 (Sunken Treasure 669 is handed in on the
#   first Booty Bay stop of forever/horde/40-50/01-stranglethorn-vale
#   instead; 670 was never handed in). About 1,900 XP at level 44, so no
#   grind stop is added; the route from Feralas to the Swamp of Sorrows
#   passes Orgrimmar and Grom'gol anyway, so those stops stay.
#
# Class quests: Warlocks pick up the Felsteed (3631, 4490) in Orgrimmar and
# Ratchet on the way in, as in the earlier Feralas guide.
#
# Class training: Orgrimmar at about 42.5 and 44 for everyone but Druids and
# Paladins, who fly to Thunder Bluff at 42.5. Riding at 40: each race's own
# riding trainer (Kildar in Orgrimmar for Orcs, Genn Fairweather on Zephras Isle for Skyborne, Xar'Ti in
# Sen'jin Village, Kar Stormsinger in Bloodhoof Village, Velma Warnam in
# Brill), all optional.
#
# Accepted here, finished later on the route: Screecher Spirits (3520,
# Steamwheedle Port, around 46.7), Deliver to MacKinley (2874) in Booty Bay
# around level 50, A Strange Request (3121), A Grim Discovery (2976) and The
# Gordunni Orb (3002) in Orgrimmar at 45, Ripple Recovery (650) in the
# Hinterlands, Improved Quality (7734) on the next Feralas visit.
#
# Optional: Find OOX-22/FE! (2766) and Rescue OOX-22/FE! (2767): the distress
# beacon drops about one kill in forty; the reward waits in Booty Bay.
#
# Left out: Pearl Diving (705: the export gathers the pearls but never hands
# them in). Speaking with Nezzliok (585, export visit 38 at Grom'gol) is done
# earlier, on the Zul'Mamwe loop of forever/horde/40-50/01-stranglethorn-vale.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- To Orgrimmar

step Fly to Grom'gol
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  tip Ride back north-west from Misty Reed Post to Stonard and fly to Grom'gol.
  fly "Grom'gol"

step Zeppelin to Orgrimmar
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip The Orgrimmar zeppelin leaves from the tower beside Grom'gol; it lands just outside Orgrimmar's main gate.
  goto 31.4,29.9 "Zeppelin tower"

step Orgrimmar
  zone Orgrimmar
  train class only Warrior,Hunter,Rogue,Priest,Shaman,Mage,Warlock
  accept 3631 only Warlock              -- Zevrost, Cleft of Shadow

step Riding at 40
  only Orc,Skyborne
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Riding needs level 40 and costs 100 gold; learning it gives you a mount. Kildar teaches Orcs in the Valley of Honor, by Ogunaro Wolfrunner's kennel. Skyborne learn it from Genn Fairweather at the Fairweather Stables in Valanaar on Zephras Isle, with a Galestrider: the skyboat to the isle leaves the cliffs south of Skywatcher Plateau, north of Thunder Bluff, about every five minutes. Your race's other mounts are 20 gold each: Collectibles, Mounts · Level 40 has a guide for each.
  train 4752 only Orc optional          -- Kildar, riding trainer
  note "Wolves: Ogunaro Wolfrunner, beside Kildar." only Orc
  note "Riding and Galestriders: Genn Fairweather, at the Fairweather Stables in Valanaar on Zephras Isle." only Skyborne

step Riding at 40
  only Troll
  zone Durotar
  tip Riding needs level 40 and costs 100 gold; learning it gives you a mount. Each race learns it from its own race's trainer: yours is Xar'Ti in Sen'jin Village on the Durotar coast, with Zjolnir's raptors (20 gold each) beside him. Another race's trainer (Kildar in Orgrimmar) teaches you only once you are Exalted with his city.
  train 7953 optional                   -- Xar'Ti, riding trainer
  note "Raptors: Zjolnir, beside Xar'Ti in Sen'jin Village."

step Riding at 40
  only Tauren
  zone Mulgore
  tip Riding needs level 40 and costs 100 gold; learning it gives you a mount. Each race learns it from its own race's trainer: yours is Kar Stormsinger in Bloodhoof Village, with Harb Clawhoof's kodos (20 gold each) beside him. Another race's trainer (Kildar in Orgrimmar) teaches you only once you are Exalted with his city.
  train 3690 optional                   -- Kar Stormsinger, riding trainer
  note "Kodos: Harb Clawhoof, beside Kar Stormsinger in Bloodhoof Village."

step Riding at 40
  only Undead
  zone Tirisfal Glades
  tip Riding needs level 40 and costs 100 gold; learning it gives you a mount. Each race learns it from its own race's trainer: yours is Velma Warnam in Brill, with Zachariah Post's skeletal horses (20 gold each) beside her. Another race's trainer (Kildar in Orgrimmar) teaches you only once you are Exalted with his city.
  train 4773 optional                   -- Velma Warnam, riding trainer
  note "Skeletal horses: Zachariah Post, beside Velma Warnam in Brill."

step Thunder Bluff
  only Druid,Paladin
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Your trainer is in Thunder Bluff: Turak Runetotem (Druids) on Elder Rise, Alodan the Hopeful (Paladins). Fly there from Gadgetzan, then back to Gadgetzan.
  fly "Thunder Bluff"
  train class

step Ratchet for the Felsteed
  only Warlock
  zone The Barrens
  fly "Ratchet"
  turnin 3631                           -- Strahad Farsan
  accept 4490
  turnin 4490

step Fly to Freewind Post
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Fly to Freewind Post, ride down the lift east of the post and across the salt flats, then south into Tanaris.
  fly "Freewind Post"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Gadgetzan and the Wastewander

step Gadgetzan
  zone Tanaris
  tip Gadgetzan is the walled goblin town just past the Tanaris border.
  getfp "Gadgetzan" npc 7824            -- Bulkrek Ragefist
  turnin 2864                           -- Tran'rek
  accept 2875 object 150075             -- the Wanted Poster in the square
  accept 1690                           -- Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
  accept 1707                           -- Spigot Operator Luglunket

step Eastern Wastewander camps
  tip The bandits and thieves camp in the dunes east of Gadgetzan. Every Wastewander can carry a water pouch: keep ten, five for each of Luglunket's bounties.
  kill 5618 quest 1690.1
  kill 5616 quest 1690.2
  collect 8483 quest 1707.1
  collect 8483 x10                      -- water pouches in your bags

step Gadgetzan
  turnin 1690                           -- Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
  accept 1691
  turnin 1707                           -- Spigot Operator Luglunket
  accept 1878
  turnin 1878

step Southern Wastewander camps
  tip The shadow mages, rogues and assassins camp south-east of Gadgetzan.
  kill 5617 quest 1691.3
  kill 5615 quest 1691.1
  kill 5623 quest 1691.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Steamwheedle Port

step Steamwheedle Port
  tip Ride north-east to the goblin harbour on the coast.
  accept 8365                           -- Haughty Modiste
  accept 3520                           -- Yeh'kinya: the screechers live in Feralas
  turnin 2872                           -- Stoley
  accept 2873
  accept 8366                           -- Security Chief Bilgewhizzle

step Lost Rigger Cove
  tip South along the coast, the Southsea pirates hold the cove. Andre Firebeard and the stolen cargo are on the docks at its far end. Any pirate can drop a hat, the kidnappers most often.
  kill 7855 quest 8366.1
  kill 7856 quest 8366.2
  kill 7857 quest 8366.3
  kill 7858 quest 8366.4
  collect 20519 quest 8365.1
  collect 9246 quest 2875.1 @73.4,47.1
  collect 9244 quest 2873.1 @72.1,46.7

step Steamwheedle Port
  turnin 2873                           -- Stoley
  accept 2874                           -- for Booty Bay, around level 50
  turnin 2875                           -- Security Chief Bilgewhizzle
  turnin 8366
  turnin 8365                           -- Haughty Modiste

step Gadgetzan
  tip Ride back west to Gadgetzan.
  turnin 1691                           -- Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
  vendor nearest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Camp Mojache

step Fly to Freewind Post
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Fly to Freewind Post, then ride west through the canyons past Whitereach Post; the road climbs into the Feralas jungle and on to Camp Mojache.
  fly "Freewind Post"

step Camp Mojache
  zone Feralas
  getfp "Camp Mojache" npc 8020         -- Shyn
  sethome "Camp Mojache" npc 7737       -- Innkeeper Greul
  accept 2862                           -- Hadoken Swiftstrider
  accept 2973                           -- Krueg Skullsplitter
  accept 2975                           -- Rok Orhan
  accept 2987                           -- Orwin Gizzmick
  accept 3121                           -- Witch Doctor Uzer'i: for Orgrimmar, around level 45
  accept 2822                           -- Jangdor Swiftstrider

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The north

step Woodpaw north camp
  tip The Woodpaw gnolls camp in the hills just north-west of Mojache; any of them can drop a mane.
  collect 9237 quest 2862.1

step Gordunni Outpost
  tip North of the gnolls the ogres hold a hilltop outpost; pull the ogre-magi to you. The cobalt is in the dirt mounds around the outpost, and the scroll lies on the ground inside it.
  kill 5229 quest 2975.1
  kill 5232 quest 2975.3
  kill 5237 quest 2975.2
  collect 9463 quest 2987.1
  collect 9370 "Gordunni Scroll"
  accept 2978

step Camp Mojache
  turnin 2862                           -- Hadoken Swiftstrider
  accept 2863                           -- Alpha Strike: one hour from now
  turnin 2975                           -- Rok Orhan
  turnin 2978
  accept 2979
  accept 2980
  turnin 2987                           -- Orwin Gizzmick

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- West and south of Mojache

step Sprite darters and Woodpaw alphas
  tip The sprite darters flit over the grove just west of Mojache; nearly every one drops a wing. The Woodpaw alphas lead the camps south-west of it: kill them within the hour.
  collect 9369 quest 2973.1
  kill 5258 quest 2863.1

step Camp Mojache
  turnin 2863                           -- Hadoken Swiftstrider
  accept 2902
  turnin 2973                           -- Krueg Skullsplitter
  accept 2974

step Grimtotem camp
  tip The Grimtotem tauren camp beside the sprite darters' grove; raiders, naturalists and shamans all carry horns.
  collect 9460 quest 2974.1

step Woodpaw battle map
  tip The battle map lies in the Woodpaw camp south of Mojache.
  turnin 2902
  accept 2903

step Camp Mojache
  turnin 2974                           -- Krueg Skullsplitter
  accept 2976                           -- for Orgrimmar, around level 45
  turnin 2903                           -- Hadoken Swiftstrider
  accept 7730
  accept 7731

step The Writhing Deep
  tip The Zukk'ash hive burrows into the hills south-east of the camp; Stinglasher waits in its deepest chamber.
  collect 18961 quest 7730.1
  collect 18962 quest 7731.1 @75.6,60.9

step Southern Gordunni ruins
  tip Ride west from the hive to the ogre ruins below Feral Scar Vale. Shamans, warlocks and maulers fill them; the Mage-Lords at the southern end carry the orb.
  kill 5234 quest 2980.3
  kill 5240 quest 2980.2
  kill 5236 quest 2980.1
  collect 9371 quest 2979.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- West: screechers and OOX-22/FE

step Rogue Vale screechers
  tip Ride west into the middle of Feralas. Kill a Rogue Vale Screecher, use Yeh'kinya's Bramble on its body and kill the spirit that rises.
  use 10699 "Yeh'kinya's Bramble" @45.0,38.0
  kill 8612 quest 3520.1

step Feral Scar Vale
  tip The yetis den in Feral Scar Vale, beside the robot's cave; every yeti there can drop a thick hide.
  collect 8973 quest 2822.1

step Homing Robot OOX-22/FE
  tip Only with the distress beacon: any beast, gnoll or ogre in Feralas can drop it, about one kill in a hundred; use it to start the quest. The robot sits in a small cave on the north side of Feral Scar Vale. Escort it to the dock on the Forgotten Coast; yetis and gorillas ambush you on the way. Its reward waits in Booty Bay for a later visit.
  accept 2766 optional
  turnin 2766 optional
  accept 2767 optional
  complete 2767 optional

step Hearth to Camp Mojache
  hearth "Camp Mojache"

step Camp Mojache
  turnin 7730                           -- Hadoken Swiftstrider
  turnin 7731
  vendor nearest
  turnin 2822                           -- Jangdor Swiftstrider
  accept 7734                           -- the Rage Scar yetis, on the next visit to Feralas
  turnin 2979                           -- Rok Orhan
  turnin 2980
  accept 3002                           -- for Orgrimmar, around level 45

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Back east

step Orgrimmar
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Fly to Orgrimmar. The Droffers brothers run their shop in the Drag.
  fly "Orgrimmar"
  accept 649                            -- Dran Droffers
  turnin 649                            -- Malton Droffers
  accept 650                            -- for the Hinterlands, around level 48
  train class only Warrior,Hunter,Rogue,Priest,Shaman,Mage,Warlock

step Zeppelin to Grom'gol
  zone Durotar
  tip The Grom'gol zeppelin leaves from the tower just north-east of Orgrimmar's main gate.
  goto 50.7,12.9 "Zeppelin tower"

step Fly to Stonard
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip Thysta, the flight master, stands just east of the zeppelin tower. Fly to Stonard: the next guide starts there.
  fly "Stonard"
